{
  "name": "TestReportMasksSensitiveVariablesJunit",
  "comment": "Companion to TestReportMasksSensitiveVariables — same fixture, but with\nformat='junit' so the committed junit.xml snapshot can be eyeballed.\nProves the JUnit XML path also masks [Sensitive] PrivateKey — BuildJUnit\nemits run.Error?.Message directly, so AssertionError.Message itself must\nbe sanitised (not just the structured JSON envelope).",
